  "worked_solution": "To determine whether a function $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=2,$ we need to check whether the right-sided limit is equal to the function value.\n\nThe function plotted below has a discontinuity at $x=2,$ but is right-continuous at $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945035/assets/b0c5521372b10882b6f5357cb678aef1274df935e7626bec930e3e084674ba62.png)\n\nIndeed, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x)=1=f(2).\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)$ is right-continuous at $x=2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
